// insanitybit/greeter — a tiny, zero-authority demo rune published from CI.
//
// It exists to prove the trusted-publishing path end to end: a GitHub Actions
// workflow mints an OIDC identity token for audience `coven-registry` and lets
// `witchy pm publish` upload this rune to the hosted coven registry. The rune
// itself needs no runtime capabilities — its whole surface is data-only,
// so the server's recomputed footprint is empty (`[capabilities] runtime = []`).

// Greet `name`, or the world when no name is given.
pub fn greet(name: String) -> String:
    if name.is_empty():
        "Hello, world!"
    else:
        "Hello, ${name}!"
